<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up to 19.02 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up to 19.02 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising 71 basis points to 19.02 percent, and rates are also seen rising at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     18.31	    19.02		   + 71 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     20.78	    21.27		   + 49 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    21.78	    22.00		   + 22 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     22.99	    23.06		   +  7 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 (2330 GMT)</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +%25 7289559))</p>
</text>
